// tests/bit/releasesurface.bit's allowlist (#3039).
//
// One line per INTENTIONAL stdlib API break, so it survives as a reviewable
// record instead of a silently-typed conventional-commit `!`:
//
//     <module> <symbol> <removed|changed> <#ticket>
//
// <module>  the import path ("std/http"), not the filesystem path
// <symbol>  the bare name as tests/bit/releasesurface.bit's parser reports
//           it: "Exchange.request" for a field/method, "newSha256" for a
//           free function
// <ticket>  REQUIRED, must look like "#1234" — the change this file exists
//           to make reviewable, not merely permitted
//
// Comments start a line with "//"; blank lines are ignored.
//
// The four changes that shipped unannounced in 0.1.16 — the ones this gate
// exists to have caught — are documented in the harness's own header
// comment rather than listed here, so this file only ever names a break
// still pending the NEXT release.
//
// `File.readAll` went `string` -> `string!` because the non-fallible form
// could not report an I/O error at all: a failed lseek, a failed allocation
// and a genuinely empty file all returned "". #2996 made the runtime flag
// observable and #3065 shipped the symbol that made it reachable, so the
// signature had to change for the error to have anywhere to go. Trading a
// silent wrong answer for a compile-time break is the right way round
// pre-1.0, and `readFile` propagates it with `?` so most callers only add
// one character. This gate went red on merged `main` while both contributing
// branches were green — neither ran it, because `gate.sh` refused their diff
// with exit 3 and the agent hand-picked gates instead.
std/fs File.readAll changed #2996
